  </section>

  <!-- ================ 6. mid-page catch ================ -->
  <!-- The closing form sits at ~82% of the page. This is the same ask at the
       point the visitor has just read how the work runs — the moment the
       process makes sense is the moment to act on it, and waiting three more
       sections to offer that costs the ones who don't scroll.
       Two fields, ghost button: it is a catch, not the main event. The hero and
       the closing form keep the page's two .btn--filled slots (§7.3). -->
  <section class="mid-ask" id="ask" data-section="mid_ask">
    <div class="container mid-ask__grid">
      <div>
        {/* Deliberately NOT "not ready to put a time on the calendar?" — the
            escape link ten percent above says exactly that, and the two read as
            a stutter. This one also promises only what the two fields can
            deliver: compact has no message box, so it says we'll reach out,
            not "tell us what's going on". */}
        <h2 class="mid-ask__head">Would you rather we reached out?</h2>
        <p class="mid-ask__body">
          Leave your name and email and we’ll get in touch within one business day to understand what you need and how we can help.
        </p>
      </div>
      <LeadForm source="home_mid" variant="compact" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===================== 7. Pulse strip ===================== -->
  <!-- The one section that does NOT route to the Pulse Check (§7.2): it routes
       to Pulse and to subscribe. -->
  <section class="section section--dark pulse-strip" data-section="pulse">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pulse-strip__top">
        <div>
          <h2 class="pulse-strip__masthead">Pulse</h2>
          <p class="pulse-strip__tagline">
